refresh = r'''## Refreshed Justice-specific assessment of the additional material

All eight retain their recorded judgment and their complete joins to the common grounds as now expressly qualified. The following conclusions supplement the full individual rows above and identify why each material source addition does or does not change a commitment. They are decisional conclusions, not fictional conference exchanges.

| Justice | Polleys: capacity, efforts, medical proof and duration | Timken: domestic review, compulsion and international argument |
|---|---|---|
| Stevens | His Lamie concurrence's attention to context supports reading the stipulation with the actual earnings findings and the move with the later employment and repayment history. The new consolidation, deferral and negotiation facts reinforce good faith. Ordinary proof and a realistic significant period remain sufficient; the statute does not prescribe the concurrence's medical and full-duration conditions. Affirmance and full join remain. | His Mead and Barnhart joins support resolving the domestic challenge rather than using §3512(c) to foreclose it. He rejects compulsory zeroing where the calculation language permits another reading, and joins affirmance after considering the report's all-transactions argument without adopting categorical fairness irrelevance. |
| O'Connor | Her Hood Part III and Lamie joins preserve the debtor's genuine burden. The stipulation removes total inability as a permissible premise but does not negate impaired earnings. The actual work, housing and lender efforts answer the move and nonpayment objections. Reliable evidence is required, but no statutory special medical or twenty-year expert-proof condition is added. Result and complete join remain. | She joins the available domestic-law channel and the concrete delegated choice. The report's investigation setting and the entry-based review matter to its persuasive application; nonbinding status alone does not dispose of Koyo's argument. Neither offsets nor zeroing is compelled by this text. Affirmance remains on permission. |
| Scalia | His authored-position evidence remains the full Lamie join: enforce the condition actually enacted. Neither a medical-disability predicate nor a mandatory expert forecast spanning every loan year appears in it. The stipulation is honored, and the full financial and lender record establishes durable inability and actual efforts without a general equitable dispensation. No vote or join changes. | His Mead dissent and Barnhart join permit the concrete deference rationale; they do not require evasion of the domestic merits. He joins rejection of the §3512(c) bar because the legal claim arises under domestic law. Exceeds is compatible with positive treatment without making it mandatory. He accepts considered persuasive use of the report while withholding binding domestic effect. |
| Kennedy | Hood and Lamie support a real showing without new statutory barriers. The ability to hold some work is legally distinct from adequate income; the supported functional limitations, payment term and cooperation show the required persistence and good faith. No missing expert-proof requirement justifies remand. Affirmance and full common join remain. | His Mead and Haggar approach requires independent threshold and boundary adjudication: domestic review is available, actual delegation exists and the fair-comparison text remains relevant. The report does not resolve the administrative-review issue, and the statutory signed-difference possibility defeats compulsion. He retains affirmance on the bounded method. |
| Souter | His Hood opinion requires the statutory merits showing rather than a medical label. His Lamie joins support consideration of all relevant context: the stipulation and voluntary move are addressed, while supported limitations, constrained expenses, later employment and lender efforts establish the rule's actual conditions. The concurrence's evidentiary concern reinforces reliability without adding a special proof rule. Result and joins remain. | His Barnhart opinion directly supports distinguishing permission from exclusivity. The §3512(c) defense fails against a domestic statutory claim, and the WTO reasoning receives persuasive analysis. He joins the narrower fairness holding rather than the lower court's categorical exclusion and finds the chosen review method permissible. |
| Thomas | Lamie's text-first rule supports rejecting both an equitable waiver and extra-statutory medical or whole-loan certainty requirements. The stipulation would defeat a premise of inability to retain any work, which this refreshed ruling expressly does not use. Earning impairment and the complete efforts record independently sustain the required conclusion. He retains affirmance and the qualified common ground. | His Mead, Barnhart and Lamie joins support the specific statutory cause, actual agency assignment and text's limits. A domestic-law claim is not barred by §3512(c); mathematical negative differences prevent a compelled-zeroing rule. The report does not control and its persuasive consideration does not render the method impermissible here. No change of vote or join. |
| Ginsburg | Her Hood and Lamie joins support application of the statutory condition to the debtor and her dependent. The more complete efforts record materially strengthens the reason for rejecting bad faith. She treats the stipulation accurately and refuses to convert valid medical evidence requirements into a categorical disability prerequisite or a prediction covering the whole loan. Affirmance and full join remain. | Her Mead and Barnhart joins support hearing the statutory appeal and evaluating the report's fairness argument on its merits. She joins rejection of compulsory zeroing and of compulsory offsets on this record, with no assertion that nonbinding international reasoning is irrelevant or that fairness never concerns aggregation. |
| Breyer | His Hood and dual Lamie joins support a workable, evidence-based application. The twenty-year obligation gives the persistence inquiry concrete scale, while the supported findings permit a realistic forecast without certainty throughout that period. The move, efforts and lender dealings show actual adjustment to limited earning prospects. He retains the complete rule and affirmance without adding a new expert-proof condition. | His Mead and Barnhart joins favor reasoned permissible administration within the actual task. Koyo's domestic appeal must be heard. The all-transactions alternative is intelligible, but the report does not conclusively govern this review, and the statute permits the agency's different method. Neither longstanding practice nor lack of binding international effect alone supplies the result. |

**Exact effect of the refresh.** Polleys retains eight affirmance votes and the realistic three-part rule. Its application now expressly honors the capacity stipulation, considers the departure from better-paying work, relies on actual consolidation/deferral/negotiation efforts, and rejects the proposed special medical and entire-loan proof requirements while preserving ordinary evidence and burden rules. The debtor-and-dependents conjunction is controlling. Timken retains eight affirmance votes but now expressly decides that §3512(c) does not bar the domestic statutory appeal, rejects the proponents' mandatory-zeroing argument, and makes clear that the persuasive fairness/WTO argument was considered. No Associate adopts categorical fairness irrelevance or reaches §3533 preclusion. No separate writing or fractured common ground is required by these refreshed commitments.

'''
